i was thinking about data filters, compost shims.
 <% shim Yaml $yamldata %> ... <% /shim %>

brings that parsed yaml data structure into the global hash,
till the end tag.

More verbosely
 <% shim Yaml -file $file -namespace shim %> ... <% /shim %>

parses $file and roots the namespace in 'shim'..
  <% $shim.config %>

also, the pulling in shimed data as a template object method
  $template->set_shim( 'Yaml', $data );

there could be shims for...
  DBI, XML, Yaml, Bdb, CSV,
  splitting stdin on columns/fields,
  splitting stdin on simple matches,
  splitting log files, 

parser should catch errors like <$ switch %>
and nonexistant parameters,

report em early - with line numbers


